A||||3||Cooter||What is up with Fiero Heaven?
Z||000000||Cooter||09-05-99||08:12 PM||||Have any of y'all tried to get in touch with Fiero Heaven? I was going to buy some parts a while back and made phone contact, but now just get a machine. I have e-mailed questions, but never get a response. I was wondering if someone had actually got anything from them and if they were still in business.
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-99||08:22 PM||||There was once a "fiero specialist" scrap yard in Allentown, PA, but they also can no longer be reached.<p>There are a bunch of people trying to make a quick buck off what they see as a resto/retro fad. Many Fiero sites appear to be the same. I've seen only a few sites, like Kick Hill Farm, that seem genuine in the effort to keep the Fiero on the road. As yet I can find no-one who is unhappy with Kick Hill. Their posted pricing is in line with most decent salvage yards, and they have things we all really need put aside. They are one of the very few places I bet where you can find 87-88 4 cyls waiting to be dropped in. They have whole v6 packages to drop in for less than a grand.
Z||000002||Gokart||09-06-99||04:42 AM||||Cooter, I was just up on their site Saturday. Was noticing their new product, GT quarter window replacements. I've never purchased anything myself from them, but I'd question their reliability just by noticing how long it's been taking them to finish their site and the infrequent "updates"!
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||09-06-99||10:09 AM||||Yeah ogre! I agree. It is hard to beat Kick hill, when it comes to Fiero parts. Top notch service. Bob is a first rate guy.
